# Database and connections

Schema lives in init SQL (`datatalk-db-init/postgres/02_init_idempotent.sql`, `03_projects_table.sql`) and in runtime `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` (no versioned migrations).

- A schema change needs both the init script and a plan for an existing Docker volume (init does not re-run).
- Qualify schema names (`datatalk_meta`, `pa_upload`). Do not create tables on an implicit `search_path`.
- Connection secrets: write only `password_enc` when encryption is available (`canUseEncryption()`). Never log secrets. `GET` connections must not return plaintext passwords.
- Source of truth for connections is `datatalk_meta.connections`, not `connection_profiles` / `connection_presets`.
- Uploads: `materializeToPostgres.ts` currently types every column as `TEXT` (I12). `connectionId` is resolved by name (`Local Postgres`) — do not assume it is the same database without checking.
- Do not run migrations or writes against the owner's volumes. Isolated test data only.
